# netsurf: a scratch document's querySelector finds what was appended
# to it (patch 293)
# Generated 2026-10-14
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 292)
#
# Found on the way in patch 279 and recorded in its Doc 10 entry: a
# document from document.implementation.createHTMLDocument answered
# querySelector with null and querySelectorAll with [] -- not just for
# its own structure, but for nodes a script appended to it afterwards,
# which is the whole point of a scratch document (sanitizers and
# template code build a fragment in one and then query it). The two
# were stubs in the bridge's document.implementation stand-in and
# nothing ever replaced them: patch 246 gave the stand-in documents a
# real getElementsByTagName (the DOMPurify fix) but left the query
# stubs in place.
#
# The patch-246 "hat" the stand-ins wear now also answers
# querySelector / querySelectorAll, from the document's own tree like
# its getElementsByTagName: the documentElement's live query (which
# walks the tree as it is now, so later appends are found), with the
# root itself counted when it matches -- a real document's
# querySelectorAll('*') includes its html element, an element's does
# not. DOMParser documents wear the same hat and get the same answer;
# theirs now also comes from their own tree rather than the bridge's
# per-document stub.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-scratch-qsa.html (SCRATCHQSA 6/6 in the
# simulator and in a reference browser -- Firefox/Camoufox, for the
# reason patch 292's header gives). The checks: a fresh scratch
# document finds its own head and body; a node appended after
# creation is found by class, by id and by a descendant selector; a
# second append is counted too, so the answer is live, not a
# snapshot; a DOMParser document answers querySelector as well.
# JS-scratch-doc.html stays SCRATCHDOC 6/6. Simulator only; the vita
# cross-build was not run (no vitaSDK on this VM). Device
# expectation is in Doc 10.
#
# Decline conditions: when a scratch document becomes a real second
# document (its own libdom tree the bridge queries natively), the
# hat's answers should be deleted in favour of the native ones.
#
diff --git a/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.js b/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.js
--- a/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.js
+++ b/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.js
@@ -2653,6 +2653,30 @@
 		try {
 			PV(doc).__vbHat = true;
 			doc.getElementsByTagName = function (t) { return byTag(this, t); };
+			/* VitaBrowser patch 293: the createHTMLDocument stand-in
+			 * also wore stub querySelector / querySelectorAll that
+			 * answered null / [] forever (found on the way in patch
+			 * 279), so a node a script appended to its scratch
+			 * document could never be found again. Answer from the
+			 * document's own tree instead, like byTag above: the
+			 * root's live query, with the root itself counted when
+			 * it matches (a document's querySelectorAll('*') finds
+			 * its html too). DOMParser documents wear the same hat
+			 * and get the same answer. */
+			doc.querySelectorAll = function (s) {
+				var root = this.documentElement;
+				if (!root || typeof root.querySelectorAll !== 'function') return [];
+				var out = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll(s));
+				try {
+					if (typeof root.matches === 'function' && root.matches(s))
+						out.unshift(root);
+				} catch (e) { /* */ }
+				return out;
+			};
+			doc.querySelector = function (s) {
+				var r = this.querySelectorAll(s);
+				return r.length ? r[0] : null;
+			};
 			if (typeof doc.getElementsByClassName !== 'function' ||
 			    !doc.documentElement)
 				doc.getElementsByClassName = function (c) {
